---
import { MessageSquare, Users, ArrowUpRight, ShieldCheck, Upload } from '@lucide/astro';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import { repositoryUrl, bookHref } from '../data.mjs';
const { book = null } = Astro.props;
const href = route => bookHref(book, route);
---
<Shell active="community" title="Community" book={book}><section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">{book?.config.name ?? 'CONTRIBUTE & ASK'}</p><h1>Share What Moves the Team Forward.</h1><p>Ask questions, get feedback, and contribute useful resources to the playbook.</p></section><section class="community-content"><div><MessageSquare size={34} /><h2>The Playbook Conversation</h2><p>Announcements, technical examples, Q&amp;A, and lessons learned belong in the hub's shared GitHub Discussions. Include the playbook name in your topic.</p>{repositoryUrl ? <a class="button" href={`${repositoryUrl}/discussions`} rel="noreferrer">Ask a Question or Share Feedback<ArrowUpRight size={18} /></a> : <p class="muted">Discussions becomes available after the owner provisions this instance.</p>}<p class="access-notice"><ShieldCheck size={18} />A GitHub sign-in and accepted repository invitation are required. Viewing this website does not grant repository access.</p></div><aside><Upload size={29} /><h2>Contribute a Resource</h2><p>Share a presentation, practical guide, or implementation example with the team.</p><a class="button button-outline" href={href('contribute/')}><Upload size={16} />Add a Resource</a><details class="community-access"><summary>Invitations and Access</summary><p>The repository owner can invite named GitHub users, check pending invitations, and revoke access through GitHub.</p>{repositoryUrl && <a class="text-link" href={`${repositoryUrl}/settings/access`} rel="noreferrer"><Users size={16} />Manage Repository Access<ArrowUpRight size={16} /></a>}<p class="access-notice">Personal-account private repositories grant collaborators write access. Read-only partner participation requires an organization-owned repository.</p><p class="muted">Revocation cannot remove material someone has already downloaded.</p></details></aside></section></Shell>